# Decision 143: a build-sized pile of air fills must not starve real
# destruction events. Tick 0 carves a stone mass with a map-wide fill (a
# build: no event) and a lattice of 1400 px corridors and 1300 px shafts
# (26 events, more connectivity clusters than one tick's 1 ms budget runs,
# each crossing the others' regions; the blocks between them come loose
# as bodies). At tick 60 a pillar in a room at the lower right is cut; the
# slab on it must come loose and fall: the census at tick 151 finds no
# stone where it was. On main the corridors' events stayed queued forever
# (each waited while any queued cluster overlapped its footprint):
# hundreds of connectivity runs, 21 events still queued at the end, and
# the slab never fell (1000 stone cells at tick 151).
